207
00:21:55.000 --> 00:21:59.600
A correct repair changes runtime
causality, not just an assertion.

208
00:21:59.600 --> 00:22:04.200
Research, review, and validation can all
start from the same

209
00:22:04.200 --> 00:22:08.800
input revision because none consumes
another branch's output. Parent still

210
00:22:08.800 --> 00:22:13.400
waits for all three. Therefore a required
failure still prevents

211
00:22:13.400 --> 00:22:18.000
approval, only parent authority may
approve, and the final result

212
00:22:18.000 --> 00:22:22.600
cannot race ahead of missing evidence. If
you removed a

213
00:22:22.600 --> 00:22:27.200
parent dependency to make the test appear
faster, restore it.

214
00:22:27.200 --> 00:22:31.800
That weakens the semantic join. If you
changed fixture delays,

215
00:22:31.800 --> 00:22:36.400
labels, or expected values, restore them.
Those changes do not

216
00:22:36.400 --> 00:22:41.000
